"The kernel mints the 185 involvement links` readings with the Text and Predicate the metamodel makes mandatory, so ka:allowed_extra holds those 185 and 185 rows today lacks. FINDINGS, WHERE THE PAPER SAYS TODAY IS WRONG. V is over all of C_S (def:violation, thm:complete), and today`s base breaks two of its own mandatories, each for the 185 involvement links whose readings today`s reflection mints (rAPIIsInvolvedInAPIAcceptsObjectTypeAsParameter and the rest): Each Reading has some Text (MC:e:ReadingHasText#1) and each Reading is used by some Predicate (MC:e:ReadingIsUsedByPredicate#1). Today`s gate does not check them. The kernel`s own reflection mints those readings with their Text and Predicate, so neither finding is a violation of the kernel`s V, and ka:v_law again allows nothing unaccounted.",
